## Interface conventions

{% include 'interface-conventions.md' %}

## What to populate

- `sections` — required sections per interface-conventions.md
  (Invocation, Branches, etc.).
- `files` — `references/*.md` per branch plus example pages.
- `rationale` — at most ~5 sentences or bullets: decisions
  made (selection criteria, branching strategy, surface area)
  and alternatives rejected. Nothing else.

## Output construction

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loom/scripts/loom.sh
WD={{ run.workdir }}

$LOOM output init "$WD" --task design-author

$LOOM output add "$WD" --task design-author \
    --set frontmatter.name=demo \
    --set frontmatter.type=interface \
    --set 'frontmatter.description=...' \
    --set 'sections.0.heading=Invocation' \
    --set 'sections.0.outline=...' \
    --set 'sections.1.heading=Branches' \
    --set 'sections.1.outline=...' \
    --set 'files.0.path=references/branch-a.md' \
    --set 'files.0.purpose=...' \
    --set 'files.0.content_outline=...' \
    --set rationale='Branching strategy and selection criteria...'
```

Syntax: arrays use dotted numeric indices (`files.0.path`,
`files.1.path`); `.` nests. The writer validates the whole
document after every `output add`, so required sibling fields
(e.g. `path` + `purpose` + `content_outline` of one file) MUST
land in the same call.
